This is a list of bugs in the past, which can not simply be mapped to an
automated unit test. Therefore this list should be worked through before any
release of JamMt.

General tests of the user interface
	[_] Open display settings and change y and y2 axis from dropdown list. Close and open again.
		Were the settings remembered correctly?
	[_] Add a substrate to the plot. Remove it immediately.
		Is the beam updated correctly?
	[_] Open the beam analyzer manager. Add two beam analyzers. Click Edit.
		Does the edit dialog pop up correctly?
	[_] Start JamMt and immediately press File -> Reset.
		There should be no error output on the terminal.
	[_] Open display settings and enlarge the x range.
		Is the plot updated correctly?
	[_] Add a lens and move it to z != 0.0. Change this lens to a predefined one.
		The position should not be changed.
	[_] Add a substrate to the plot. Then change it to a thin lens.
		Is the lens updated correctly?

